course: dictionary
lesson: 15099
title: Rower
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rower is a person who moves a boat through the water using oars. «The rower pulled hard on the oars and the boat slid across the lake.» The words around rower tell you what a rower does: pulls the oars through the water.
explain: The word can also mean a rowing machine in a gym. «After school, Maya spent twenty minutes on the rower to get fit.» There is no water or boat in a gym, so this rower is the machine, not a person. Always check the other words around the word.
explain: To choose the right meaning, swap your meaning into the sentence. «Each rower wore a bright orange life jacket.» Does "each person who rows wore a life jacket" still make sense? Yes, so this rower is a person in a boat.
fact: A rower moves a boat with oars, which are long poles with a flat blade at one end.
fact: Rowers can race in teams of 1, 2, 4 or 8.
fact: In a race, rowers face backwards, so they can see where they have been.
fact: Rowers wear life jackets to stay safe in case they fall into the water.
fact: A rower can also be a rowing machine, used for exercise in a gym.
exercise: «The rower pulled hard on the oars.» What is a rower in this sentence? | A bird that flies over the river | *A person who moves a boat with oars | A kind of bridge | A large fish in the lake
exercise: «Maya spent twenty minutes on the rower in the gym.» What is the rower here? | A long wooden pole | *A rowing machine used for exercise | A teacher with a whistle | A person sitting in a boat
exercise: In a race, which way do rowers face? | Forwards, towards the finish line | *Backwards, so they can see where they have been | Sideways, towards the crowd | Up at the sky
test: «The rower took the children across the river in a small boat.» What is the rower's job here? | *Carrying people across a river in a boat | Selling tickets at the gym | Painting the boat bright red | Catching fish with a net
test: Why must rowers wear life jackets? | To look smart in the race | To keep warm in the cold | *To stay safe if they fall into the water | To make the boat go faster
exam: Which sentence uses rower to mean a rowing machine? | *Dad used the rower in the gym for ten minutes | The rower wore a red helmet and waved | The rower pulled the oars through the water | Rowers race in teams of 1, 2, 4 or 8
